    <Label Name="Title" Style="Heading" Text="The Pizza Theorem" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="Explanation" Text="Pick any point on a pizza and make four straight cuts through it, each 45° from the last, so there are eight slices. Take every other slice. You get exactly half the pizza, however far from the middle the point is.\n\nThe four yellow slices: [S0.Area + S2.Area + S4.Area + S6.Area]. The four red ones: [S1.Area + S3.Area + S5.Area + S7.Area]. Half the pizza: [Pizza.Area / 2].\n\nDrag the point where the cuts meet anywhere on the pizza, or the knife around the crust to turn the cuts. The toppings stay on their slices: drag one, and it won't leave. The proof is a famous hard one; the picture is not. Each slice is an Intersection, the pizza with a wedge." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true">
      <Dependency Name="S0" />
      <Dependency Name="S2" />
